          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Extensions are central to the success of AsciiDoc because they open up the language to new use cases. Asciidoctor provides an "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "extension API"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "metadata": {
                  "rel": "noopener",
                  "window": "_blank"
                },
                "target": "https://www.rubydoc.info/gems/asciidoctor/2.0.23/Asciidoctor/Extensions"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that offers a superset of extension points. As a result, extensions in Asciidoctor are easy to write, powerful, and simple to distribute."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Asciidoctor also allows extensions to be written using the full power of a programming language (whether it be Ruby, Java, Groovy or JavaScript). You don’t have to shave yaks to get the functionality you want, and you can distribute the extension using de facto standard packaging mechanisms like gems or JARs."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
